  "findings": [
    "0.004 per cent of the stream was lost over the link, 1 packets of the 24003 the sequence numbers describe",
    "frames arrived -10.0 ms past their moment at p50, -6.1 at p95, 30.0 at p99 and 52.3 at worst, against a target of 10 ms; negative is margin in hand, and the shape is what says whether the target is short by a fixed amount every frame pays or long enough for all but a tail",
    "the jitter buffer held 10.0 ms at p50 and 10.0 ms at p99 against a 10 ms target, measured after serving each frame",
    "window by window that occupancy went from 10.0 ms at p50 in the first of 12 windows to 10.0 in the last, staying between 5.0 and 10.0; a run-wide percentile cannot be separated back into these, so whether the buffer grew during the arm is readable here and nowhere above",
    "the ring sat at 2176 frames of 4096 at p50, having been primed to 496; the difference is the 32.8 ms `AudioDeviceStart` spent getting the device going, during which the producer kept depositing and the device consumed nothing, so it is the ring's contribution to latency and it belongs to the device rather than to the link",
    "the source clock runs +0.08 ppm referred to this Mac's timebase, as this run's own per-block minima fit it, against A7's +9.29 ppm for the same pair, and THEY DISAGREE BY MORE THAN A FACTOR OF TWO, so one of the two measurements is wrong and neither may be cited until that is settled. That is a delay slope of -0.08 ppm - a fast source makes the subtracted RTP term outrun arrival time, so the two have opposite signs and both are stated because reading one as the other is how this reported a disagreement on its first radio run. Over the 120 s of stream time it is -0.01 ms of accumulated skew, which took +0.002 ms off the p99 of the raw curve and +0.007 ms off its maximum. The same fit over every arrival rather than the minima gives +2.34 ppm, and the two differing is the burst sensitivity that chose the estimator",
    "excess above this run's own best case reached 0.04 ms at p50, 3.98 at p95, 40.04 at p99 and 62.31 at worst over 24002 arrivals, with 0 of them past the 100 ms the curve reports out to; the reference is the minimum over the run and not the first packet, so this is comparable with another run's and an arrival delay anchored on one datagram is not",
    "a 5 ms target would have left 1196 frames of 24002 past their moment, 4.9829 per cent, at 597.95 a minute and 565.45 clusters a minute: clusters of 1 frames at p50, 1 at p95 and 4 at worst - 20 ms of timeline in the worst one - separated by 75 ms at p50 and 5 ms at closest",
    "a 10 ms target would have left 1182 frames of 24002 past their moment, 4.9246 per cent, at 590.95 a minute and 560.95 clusters a minute: clusters of 1 frames at p50, 1 at p95 and 3 at worst - 15 ms of timeline in the worst one - separated by 75 ms at p50 and 5 ms at closest",
    "a 20 ms target would have left 1176 frames of 24002 past their moment, 4.8996 per cent, at 587.95 a minute and 559.95 clusters a minute: clusters of 1 frames at p50, 1 at p95 and 3 at worst - 15 ms of timeline in the worst one - separated by 75 ms at p50 and 5 ms at closest"
